.TH CHTTPCLIENT_SET_TLS 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_set_tls \- set TLS configuration for a client
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpclient_set_tls(chttpcli cli,
                                  const chttp_tls_config_t *tls);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Copies the supplied TLS configuration into the client.  Passing NULL
restores the default (verify_peer = true, verify_host = true, system
CA bundle, no client certificate).

The strings in chttp_tls_config_t (cert_path, key_path, ca_bundle_path)
are deep-copied into client-owned buffers; the caller's originals may
be freed or reused immediately after this call returns.

cert_path/key_path/ca_bundle_path are validated for readability
lazily, at the time an HTTPS request actually needs them, rather than
here; a path that does not currently exist is accepted here without
error and only surfaces as ccol_http_tls_cert_verification_failed from
chttpclient_do/chttpclient_do_streaming once a request needs it.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cli   Client handle; must not be NULL.
tls   TLS configuration to copy, or NULL to restore defaults.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success      Configuration updated.
ccol_invalid_args cli is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR CHTTP_TLS_DEFAULT (3),
.BR create_chttpclient (3)
